  "instructions": [
    "In a large stockpot, combine pork bones, pork shoulder, onion, carrot, celery, garlic, star anise, cinnamon stick, and fennel seeds.",
    "Pour in 4 quarts of water and bring to a boil over high heat.",
    "Reduce the heat to low and simmer for 1 1/2 hours, or until the meat is tender and the broth is rich and flavorful.",
    "Strain the broth through a fine-mesh sieve into a clean pot, discarding the solids.",
    "Add fish sauce, soy sauce, and sugar to the broth and stir to combine.",
    "Bring the broth to a simmer over medium heat.",
    "Cook the rice noodles according to the package instructions and divide among bowls.",
    "Slice the pork into thin strips and add to the bowls.",
    "Ladle the hot broth over the pork and noodles, and garnish with fresh herbs and sliced scallions.",
    "Serve immediately and enjoy!",
    "Cook pork to an internal temperature of 63°C / 145°F, then rest 3 minutes before serving."
  ],
